Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — individual review draft
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-09-28
Status: Individual scene draft; whole-film pass provisionally accepted, individual author review pending

INT./EXT. OLD ASSESSMENT CENTRE/WORKROOM - DAY

Voss finds a booking for an observation room. Helen and Brian separately remember Mac bringing them after hours, the dark pane and the small girl beyond it. Their memories differ in detail but meet on the decision: Brian suspected the resemblance had been arranged; Helen knew there might still be family. They accepted anyway.

Zoe studies the plan. She goes to the building, stands outside and decides not to enter. She closes her notebook. No speech tells the audience how to judge her feeling.
